#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of primitive outputs {#overview-of-primitive-outputs}"
msgstr "Przegląd wyjść prymitywów {#overview-of-primitive-outputs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once one or more PUBs are sent to a QPU for execution and a job successfully"
" completes, the data is returned as a "
"[`PrimitiveResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult)"
" container object. The `PrimitiveResult` contains an iterable list of "
"[`PubResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult)"
" objects that contain the execution results for each PUB. For example, a job"
" submitted with 20 PUBs will return a `PrimitiveResult` object that contains"
" a list of 20 `PubResults`, one corresponding to each PUB.\n"
msgstr ""
"Po wysłaniu jednego lub więcej PUBów do QPU i pomyślnym ukończeniu zadania "
"dane są zwracane jako obiekt kontenera "
"[`PrimitiveResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PrimitiveResult)."
" `PrimitiveResult` zawiera iterowalną listę obiektów "
"[`PubResult`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.PubResult),"
" które przechowują wyniki wykonania dla każdego PUBu. Na przykład zadanie "
"zgłoszone z 20 PUBami zwróci obiekt `PrimitiveResult` zawierający listę 20 "
"obiektów `PubResult`, po jednym dla każdego PUBu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each of these `PubResult` objects possess both a `data` and an optional "
"`metadata` attribute. The `data` attribute is a customized "
"[`DataBin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.DataBin)"
" that contains the the expectation value estimates in case of the Estimator,"
" or samples of the circuit output in the case of the Sampler.\n"
msgstr ""
"Każdy z tych obiektów `PubResult` posiada zarówno atrybut `data`, jak i "
"opcjonalny atrybut `metadata`. Atrybut `data` to dostosowany obiekt "
"[`DataBin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.DataBin),"
" który zawiera oszacowania wartości oczekiwanych w przypadku Estimatora lub "
"próbki wyjścia Circuit w przypadku Samplera.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `data` attribute might also include other implementation-specific "
"information such as standard deviations. The `metadata` attribute can "
"contain additional implementation-specific information about the execution "
"of the associated PUB.\n"
msgstr ""
"Atrybut `data` może również zawierać inne informacje specyficzne dla "
"implementacji, takie jak odchylenia standardowe. Atrybut `metadata` może "
"zawierać dodatkowe informacje specyficzne dla implementacji dotyczące "
"wykonania powiązanego PUBu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following is a visual outline of the `PrimitiveResult` data structure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Poniżej przedstawiono wizualny zarys struktury danych `PrimitiveResult`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"estimator\" label=\"Estimator output\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"estimator\" label=\"Estimator output\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"    └── PrimitiveResult\n"
"        ├── PubResult[0]\n"
"        │   ├── metadata\n"
"        │   └── data  ## In the form of a DataBin object,\n"
"        |       |     ## which includes data such as the following:\n"
"        │       ├── evs\n"
"        │       │   └── List of estimated expectation values in the shape\n"
"        |       |         specified by the first pub\n"
"        │       └── stds\n"
"        │           └── List of calculated standard deviations in the\n"
"        |                 same shape as above\n"
"        ├── PubResult[1]\n"
"        |   ├── metadata\n"
"        |   └── data  ## In the form of a DataBin object,\n"
"        |       |     ## which includes data such as the following:\n"
"        |       ├── evs\n"
"        |       │   └── List of estimated expectation values in the shape\n"
"        |       |        specified by the second pub\n"
"        |       └── stds\n"
"        |           └── List of calculated standard deviations in the\n"
"        |                same shape as above\n"
"        ├── ...\n"
"        ├── ...\n"
"        └── ...\n"
"    ```\n"
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    The above is an example of data that might be returned.  The actual data returned depends on the implementation.\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"sampler\" label=\"Sampler output\">\n"
